From: programista-zacny <5969291+programista-zacny@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] init: keep persistent logcat to /data off by default

(From staging/fixes-3, patches/gts2-common/0007; that file has no header.)

[combined set, 2026-11-06] The four added lines are those of the staged
file. Regenerated because the trailing context is the comment of the
previous patch, whose wording changed (see there).
---
 rootdir/etc/init.universal5433.rc | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/rootdir/etc/init.universal5433.rc b/rootdir/etc/init.universal5433.rc
index cba69d0..534baca 100644
--- a/rootdir/etc/init.universal5433.rc
+++ b/rootdir/etc/init.universal5433.rc
@@ -673,6 +673,10 @@ service persistentLogging /system/bin/logcat -r 1024 -n 9 -f /data/.logs/log
     class core
     user system
     group system
+    # Off unless asked for: the log on /data holds whatever apps print, account data included,
+    # and rewriting 10 MB of it around the clock wears the eMMC. Switch on with
+    #   setprop persist.vendor.logcat.enabled 1
+    disabled
 
 # Note: without a "disabled" option the service above starts with class core on every boot; with
 # one (see the service) it runs only while the property below is 1.
